{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/917457-which-of-the-gamelines-speak-the-most-to-you","id":917457,"title":"Which Of The Gamelines Speak The Most To You?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-19T11:18:24-07:00","id":917457,"title":"Which Of The Gamelines Speak The Most To You?","content":"Feel free to write as much or as little as you want. I'm not feeling verbose, so I'll be brief.<br /> <br /> For me, it's gotta be Changeling. To sum it up, I love the themes of learning to deal with bad experiences, of not being defined just by what has been done to me, but what I'll do for my growth as a person. To remain capable of seeing wonders in the middle of the darkness.<br /> <br /> Honorable mention to Mage and Genius, for the themes of self-determination, knowledge-seeking and controlling your hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:42:28-07:00","id":917467,"title":"","content":"Hunter- its themes of fighting against the odds and actually winning, of bringing few points of light in the darkness, of pushing yourself beyond your limits and working together to accomplish things a single person just can't is just beautiful to me. Mage (discovering hidden secrets not meant to be known), Geist (cheating your way and creating power out of &quot;trash&quot;) and Vampire (endless attempts at clinging to the past in order to maintain your identity) are the next, on that order. Honorable mention- Immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:43:06-07:00","id":917470,"title":"","content":"That's tough. <br /> <br /> Mummy is my favorite gameline, but it doesn't /speak/ to me in any tangible way, it just happens to provide a handy excuse to revel in history and Egyptian myth. If we're looking for a game that actually has an emotional punch, I want to say Promethean; Changeling makes the list too, but (in my eyes) it's a metaphor for experiences I only know second-hand through loved ones, having been fortunate enough to never know abuse myself. <br /> <br /> Promethean, to me, is a game all about identity. It's about rejection and wanting to be normal, about building an identity for yourself and becoming comfortable in your own skin even in a world that doesn't understand you. I absolute adore that it says &quot;humanity can be fucking awful, but it's still all somehow worth it&quot; because that really is the experience of life. As someone both grapping with some gender stuff and dealing with the much more common questions of identity that come with young adulthood, the Great Work feels like a journey I'm on just as much as one of the Created.<br /> <br /> The only game that speaks to me more is Wraith, but that's a topic for the other forum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T11:49:21-07:00","id":917475,"title":"","content":"Mage and Werewolf speak the strongest to me in terms of the stories I want to play.<br /> <br /> Beast speaks the strongest to me in terms of relating to my real life experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:46:57-07:00","id":917540,"title":"","content":"Promethean definitely speaks to me the most. It was what brought me into CofD and I was, as I've said, inspired by the concept. Changeling occupies an interesting space because 1e Changeling never spoke to me but pretty much everything I've seen about 2e Changeling has. Part of that is just where I was at in my life when I first read it vs. where I am now, but a larger part is just some subtle shifts in emphasis 2e is making that make it resonate with me in a way it didn't before. As someone with a very Gnostic-informed outlook on life, there are parts of Mage and Demon that speak to me strongly, though the overall pictures both paint are not as compelling to me as Promethean or 2e Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T16:18:41-07:00","id":917606,"title":"","content":"My favorites among the ChroD set are probably Promethean, Changeling, and Hunter. I feel like I'm going to end up adding Demon and Beast to those as well, but I haven't had enough opportunities to play them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T18:29:54-07:00","id":917691,"title":"","content":"I've said this elsewhere, but I've always had a soft spot for Promethean and for the book that inspired it, Frankenstein. It always struck me as a metaphor for living with autism in some ways, and with that in mind, I appreciate that Promethean is inclined toward a good ending by the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T18:34:13-07:00","id":917696,"title":"","content":"Werewolf. Themes of living in a primal state of being that is better and worse than this modern life.<br /> <br /> Changeling. Themes of not knowing exactly where to go next in life or what you're supposed to be, and of looking for stability and security.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 06-20-2016, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T18:43:37-07:00","id":917704,"title":"","content":"Vampire, for its atmosphere of sex and murder, and its depiction of Humanity and how ones deeds can affect both how you view yourself and how people view you. The idea of the Requiem is also a strong pull for me. Werewolf calls to me more as a game of brutal dominance and savage violence, of abandonment of self control to one's 'baser' urges and the exultant feelings it can bring alongside the long-lasting regrets, as well as other impulses that never stop wanting to be acted upon. With the expansion of my family I've come to appreciate the nature of the pack a bit more, too.<br /> <br /> I feel the spirit world speaks to me, too, in its reflections, both twisted and honest, of many things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T21:29:35-07:00","id":917781,"title":"","content":"The ones that speak to me are the ones that got me into it-Werewolf, Promethean, and forever Changeling(Lost, yes, but Dreaming too).<br /> <br /> The narrative between the three(four) might speak for themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T22:23:18-07:00","id":917803,"title":"","content":"Demon, fighting an unwinnable war for what's &quot;right&quot; against evil, raging against the machine, also the tech aspects speak to me.<br /> Vampire, in the words of Godsmack, the overtones of sexual lust, power, or is it the immortality of the undead.<br /> Hunter, for similar reasons as to Demon<br /> Mage, the unending pursuit of knowledge and the arrogance of seeing yourself above others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Beast, maybe? I've yet to feel enough draw to want to run Beast, that said the idea of being able to judge and teach people lessons appeals to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T02:33:47-07:00","id":917883,"title":"","content":"<b>Werewolf</b> and <b>Changing Breeds</b>, not just because I wrote some of the source material they've named back when I was really into the Occult, but because I feel like the Werewolf stuff has some of the most character and the rawest feelings to them. I like my Tabletop RPGs to have some power-fantasy to them, and Werewolf has the most visceral portrayals of that.I also LOVE <b>Hunter</b>, because, while they make good evildoers, I like to play them as these brooding badasses who fight the actual bad-guys, because I'm into playing the &quot;good guy&quot;. I also really enjoyed a copy of <b>Midnight Roads</b> someone lent me a few years ago, and I've always wanted to do more with <b>Mage</b> and <b>Changeling</b>, but the only other WoD GMs in the area either don't invite new players, or only want to have Humans or Vampires. (Humans get old, Vampires don't enthuse me)<br /> <br /> Obviously, I'm also a big fan of <b>Dragon</b>, if we count fan-books...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":10120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","user":"RockstarRaccoon","date":". 06-20-2016, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T03:25:27-07:00","id":917902,"title":"","content":"Mage, because it tackles the issue of being removed from humanity-community shared narrative of life, and not experiencing what others experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T04:37:51-07:00","id":917948,"title":"","content":"I speak to my mage books if that counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T06:02:43-07:00","id":917972,"title":"","content":"Mummy: I've been so privileged in my lifetime that I'm practically blessed, but I feel like I've been living my life for someone else, but I don't know if that's a bad thing. The memory and decreasing power parts aren't really applicable, but I sometimes wonder if I gave up some opportunities or sacrificed my identity just because I want to maintain my easy lifestyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T08:12:13-07:00","id":918047,"title":"","content":"In mage, the relationship between magic and understanding. And in Demon its the importance of the discovery of free will and what you choose to do with it. In changeling its overcoming great trauma and reclaiming either your old life or choosing to create a new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:38:10-07:00","id":918117,"title":"","content":"Promethean for me, mostly by route of mental illness.<br /> <br /> Mummy's element of &quot;too late to be a part of the world&quot; as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T11:03:26-07:00","id":918131,"title":"","content":"Hunter, because I can see a lot of flawed people who struggle to do the most right thing in my family alone. Plus I also identify with the idea that everything you think you know about life is crap, and learning from your own closed-mindedness and mistakes to be better at what you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T13:36:02-07:00","id":918222,"title":"","content":"Vampire. All these small and large human failures and mucking around in them, causing them, committing them, seeing them. The balance of trying to get ahead and not sacrificing too much of yourself along the way. Hurting others to survive and trying to make it worth it (or make yourself believe it is worth it). I dig the theme of crime and punishment (which is easy to set up in a game of Requiem). It is also the main social game, which is one of my favourite aspects in CofD games. Finally, I dig the idea of blood-soaked eternity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T17:58:45-07:00","id":918349,"title":"","content":"Also, Demon, cause god, is there a solid reflection of today's issues in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T18:28:29-07:00","id":918356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/917457-which-of-the-gamelines-speak-the-most-to-you?p=918349#post918349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Demon, cause god, is there a solid reflection of today's issues in there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you mind elaborating on that when you have the time? I don't think I've heard you say this about Demon before.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T20:49:51-07:00","id":918415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/917457-which-of-the-gamelines-speak-the-most-to-you?p=918356#post918356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do you mind elaborating on that when you have the time? I don't think I've heard you say this about Demon before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really it's a timeless one, but it's most observed today, that being the trouble of systems. Also questions about identity in relationship to the myriad systems in our lives.<br /> <br /> Also, if you decide to ignore techgnosticism and make a really big stink over the technological aspect of the game, then the most viable reading of the game is a critique against the cult of science-fetishism that is all over the place, and that's also really cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T00:41:02-07:00","id":918479,"title":"","content":"The line that speaks to me the most is changeling. To deal with your entire world being changed forever while you still wear that mask and pretend that nothing has changed. To find you are not the only one with such a mask and that they too draw inspiration from the emotions of those that surround them. For your life to follow the path dictated by the laws of narrative for life is a long series of impossible coincidences. But what speaks to me more than the 'survivor' aspect is the fact that no matter the depths you have seen or fallen to you can rise to heights you never could have dreamt of if you had not been as low as you were.<br /> <br /> Demon speaks to me in the same vein as changing with cover but beyond that it doesn't reach the depth that changeling resonates with me.<br /> <br /> Mage resonates with how I do doubt the world's truth around me at times but I know that if I as a person were to be a mage I would descend and become one of the mad so though many things about its themes and presentation speaks to me it speaks more to my flaws that I know how to manage unlike changeling which speaks to the strengths that have allowed me to persevere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T02:19:49-07:00","id":918514,"title":"","content":"Changeling's quest to learn to trust again. Promethean's struggle for understanding what the hell &quot;being human&quot; even means. Werewolf's sense of being a sheepdog patrolling a beat around the flock, of being part of the flock and yet impossibly never really being part of it. Mage's (and Werewolf's) sense of an inevitable amount of collateral damage when one takes action, being forced to constantly confront what level of damage is acceptable and what is mere vanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:48:14-07:00","id":918601,"title":"","content":"Would be a post about &quot;why certain gamelines DON'T speak to me&quot; would be ok here? It wouldn't be a critique of the games in question or a flamebait, but a description of a dissonance clash, mostly focused on me and not the games in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T07:39:54-07:00","id":918620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/917457-which-of-the-gamelines-speak-the-most-to-you?p=918601#post918601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be a post about &quot;why certain gamelines DON'T speak to me&quot; would be ok here? It wouldn't be a critique of the games in question or a flamebait, but a description of a dissonance clash, mostly focused on me and not the games in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I figure making a different thread would be more appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T11:44:51-07:00","id":918717,"title":"","content":"Mage, for sure. I think that the genuine desire to understand the world and each other better has the potential to be one of the most noble aspirations and that if everyone shared that desire the world would be a much better place. Mage is about taking that desire too far, but that kind of curiosity is still at the core of what makes a Mage, and I like that exercising that curiosity is rewarded with real power. I also like that some of the most fundamental abilities of awakened magic (mage sight, knowing and unveiling spells) are incredibly good at finding things out and obtaining knowledge that would be impossible to gain otherwise. 5 dot spells are cool and all, but just imagine what you could learn with one dot in every Arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9001-solidork","name":"solidork","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"178"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T12:12:08-07:00","id":918734,"title":"","content":"Now that i've thought more about it there is no game in its entirety that 'speak' more to me. Instead i latch onto parts of every game. I've already spoken about mage, demon and changeling but there are elements in all the other game line that speaks to me just as much.<br /> <br /> In vampire, its in the decay both moral and social that accompany the nights of unlife. Although there are great immediate change, its more about the weight of time and the questionnable actions you take on a nightly basis to survive.<br /> <br /> In werewolf, i really like the clarity of purpose behing the hunt. Its almost a tautological truth in the sense that 'the wolf must hunt' because 'the wolf must hunt'. Now human minds will find way to complicate it (and thats cool too, another thing to explore). But, that simple purpose will always be there.<br /> <br /> In prometheans, i also like the concept of purpose, but here is not an immediate purpose like in werewolf. Here we have a journey on the long term, exhausting and frustrating, but still clear in the distance.<br /> <br /> Geist, is harder, for me its less the second chance relating with the geist and more the burden that comes with the knowledge that came with dying and the responsibilities (to be followed or avoided) that came in dealing with both the alive and the dead.<br /> <br /> Finally, with mummy i latch onto the concept of witnessing and being part of history in a way that is more exemplify than in fellow immortals like vampire. To see history, to shape it in small ways and seeing parts of the past in the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 06-21-2016, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T16:45:51-07:00","id":918850,"title":"","content":"Beast hits me in some really deep places. It's almost too easy to make the metaphorical leap from intrusive thoughts to Horrors, and the desire to be rid of them at any cost is, well, I get Heroes just as much as I get Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:15:35-07:00","id":918869,"title":"","content":"Princess the Hopeful; though I would probably be low on Belief as I struggle with trying to maintain hope. Still, the effort to maintain it is there, so at least I haven't given that up yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T00:36:43-07:00","id":918983,"title":"","content":"Changeling will always hold a special place in my heart, it's themes are... basically perfect in my eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2313-knit-i-fine","name":"Knit-I-Fine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T15:24:16-07:00","id":919346,"title":"","content":"Dang, all of the Chonicles of Darkness gamelines have had a huge impact on both my growth as a GM and a story teller, but the one that truly had an impact on my life has got to be Changeling: the Lost. <br /> <br /> I picked up that game in a point in my life where I felt truly lost in regards to my place in the world, and it's themes and stories helped give me a tiny bit of Clarity about what I should truly focus on, and what I must be willing to give up to move forward down the road of life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T04:11:25-07:00","id":919634,"title":"","content":"Mage. It brings up a lot of ideas that are important to keep in mind. The dangers of Hubris, of course, but I've always seen the Watchtowers as embodying hopeful messages, coupled with warnings (for example, the Acanthus path is a reminder that we and our decisions matter. Therefore, it is important to try and make good ones).<br /> <br /> Speaking of hope, Princess. I discovered that gameline during a difficult time, in which the world seemed like a very dark place. Reading it helped me to hold things together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","name":"RdMarquis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T15:51:02-07:00","id":925077,"title":"","content":"Number one is probably Genius. For me, while there are enough bumps and inconsistencies that keep it from being the best ChroD game, the central theme is the one that resonates with me the most, and it's why I started my remake of Awakening to incorporate the ideas of Genius more organically into ChroD. <br /> <br /> Demon is probably the canon line that fits the most with me, for a lot of reasons. The aesthetic, the weirdness, the mechanics, all of that stuff- it just speaks to me. And it handles themes of personal identity/lends itself to an SJ reading much better than either Promethean or Beast, which is something else that's super important to me. It's ultimately about fighting to be yourself, even if reality itself is against you- and unlike in Promethean, &quot;yourself&quot; can be a towering robotic colossus or a collective of disparate human identities, or conceivably anything else. <br /> <br /> Changeling is another one that really resonates with me, and although the themes aren't as personally relevant to me as those of Genius or Demon I still consider it overall the best ChroD game. <br /> <br /> I've always loved the novel Frankenstein and related to the character of The Creature more than any other fictional character, and that's why I don't like Promethean- to me, it really misses the point of the story and taints the parts that I felt a connection to. <br /> <br /> Vampire, Hunter, Mummy, Geist, and Leviathan are my other favorite lines, and while there are individual things in each of them that I can relate to a lot, I'm mostly interested in them because the mechanics/plot/settings are interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:51:49-07:00","id":925258,"title":"","content":"Probably Geist for appreciating little things even when your surrounded by darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T18:37:52-07:00","id":926199,"title":"","content":"Hunter.<br /> <br /> The stories you hear when you're a lawyer...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T20:56:48-07:00","id":926242,"title":"","content":"Vampire. It's about sex, death,vice and addiction in all its forms, human strength and frailty and not knowing which is more beautiful and which is more sad, and what else is there in the world more worthy to sit around a table and romantically ruminate about with your friends and a bottle of wine(red)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","user":"JTroy","date":". 07-04-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T22:17:07-07:00","id":926277,"title":"","content":"Vampire. I love those self-deluded pricks. I love that they play all these elaborate games and political machinations and spiritual rites, just to make sure they're the jerks who have more blood than the other jerks.<br /> <br /> Fighting for second are Mage, Demon, and Promethean, but I usually give the edge to Mage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T02:57:36-07:00","id":928031,"title":"","content":"My Top 3<br /> <br /> Changeling. There's a lot of freedom with Character Creation, Also the stories you can create with your character if not creating NPCs. <br /> <br /> Hunter. I've always have been a fan of humanity facing monsters and dangers. Be it through Will, Faith, Science. Mortals facing darkness whether to triumph or be broken by it... maybe become one with it if there not careful. It's a struggle not just against the supernatural, but also with ourselves<br /> <br /> Mage. Once a mere mortal, now given So much power. But what to do? Always like the possibilities to go above and beyond, but to remember that their still consequences to your actions. Just because you gain power, doesn't mean all your problems go away and most of the time your just gonna get more.<br /> <br /> Ultimately. Changeling is my Favorite game. But Hunters Virgil speaks to me on a deep personal level.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T17:33:39-07:00","id":928527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RdMarquis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/917457-which-of-the-gamelines-speak-the-most-to-you?p=919634#post919634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage. It brings up a lot of ideas that are important to keep in mind. The dangers of Hubris, of course, but I've always seen the Watchtowers as embodying hopeful messages, coupled with warnings (for example, the Acanthus path is a reminder that we and our decisions matter. Therefore, it is important to try and make good ones).<br /> <br /> Speaking of hope, Princess. I discovered that gameline during a difficult time, in which the world seemed like a very dark place. Reading it helped me to hold things together.</div> </div> </div> </div> What would be the hopeful messages and warnings of the other Paths, in your opinion?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T17:47:37-07:00","id":928534,"title":"","content":"For Moros, it would be<br /> Everything dies, everything changes, nothing stay the same. Nothing will last forever. Anything can be torn down by clawing at it's flaws, and be rebuilt into something new. This means that while your happiness will never last, your despair too is fleeting, and it's actually in your power to direct the change towards something good. Your current happiness will die, but use it's corpse to give birth to new one. Kill your despair and build your bright future with it's bones. Embrace the change and direct it, instead of opposing it or giving up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T13:11:13-07:00","id":928882,"title":"","content":"Vampire is kind of a weird case for me because I've always been fascinated by immortality, and vampires as a specific kind of immortality, but there isn't really anything about the vampire condition that I can personally relate to, since I'm not actually an immortal vice-ruled night creature. But I still find it super interesting, in more of a hypothetical way. The parts that &quot;speak&quot; to me most are the parts that aren't as much about addiction as about desire- the desire for immortality, or to be a better/stronger/more attractive/more popular/different person.<br /> <br /> I've always hated anything that harps on about mortality, so I'm not very interested in that as a theme in anything unless transcending it is also an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-09-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T16:29:50-07:00","id":928946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/917457-which-of-the-gamelines-speak-the-most-to-you?p=928527#post928527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What would be the hopeful messages and warnings of the other Paths, in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mastigos has quite a few. But then, so do all of the Paths. One that sticks in my mind is that everyone has a dark side, something in us that we don't like or even fear. We can't lie to ourselves about it, or wall ourselves off from other people. It's okay to be flawed. That's part of being human. We need to accept who we are, and each other, for better or worse. To confront our dark side and find a way to live with it. Or overcome it. Obviously, the ordeal to do so will be tremendously difficult, but we will be better for having made the effort.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, knowing that everyone has this dark side means that everyone has a weakness that can be exploited. The security afforded by minds, distances or walls is not absolute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7925,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","user":"RdMarquis","date":". 07-09-2016, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7925-rdmarquis","name":"RdMarquis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T09:27:39-07:00","id":933449,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Dificult question. I like all the games I've played, but the one that does speak to me the most would be Changeling. A lot of the book is very similar to things I experienced myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11165-tangledvirus","name":"TangledVirus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}